# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, and ONLY for third-party code TSan cannot see
# into. Nothing in ctbrowser is suppressed here, ever - a suppression that
# silences your own code turns a green TSan run into a decoration.
#
# The Vulkan ICD (lavapipe, and any other driver) is not instrumented, so TSan
# reports its internal mutex and allocator traffic as races. Every frame of
# those reports is inside the driver; none is in ctbrowser. Suppressing by
# LIBRARY rather than by pattern keeps that narrow: a race in our code is still
# reported even when the driver is on the stack below it.
#
# Verified by planting a race in sdl_gpu_backend and confirming it is still
# caught with these suppressions active.
# libdbus, reached through SDL's initialisation the moment a test drives the
# whole application (run_app) rather than the browser alone. The inversion is
# between two of dbus's own mutexes, taken inside
# _dbus_connection_new_for_transport; nothing in ctbrowser is on either stack.
deadlock:libdbus-1.so
mutex:libdbus-1.so
called_from_lib:libdbus-1.so

race:libvulkan_lvp.so
race:libvulkan.so
race:libLLVM
mutex:libvulkan_lvp.so
mutex:libvulkan.so
deadlock:libvulkan_lvp.so
called_from_lib:libvulkan_lvp.so
called_from_lib:libvulkan.so

# ANGLE AND SWIFTSHADER, which are what a -DCTBROWSER_WITH_ANGLE=ON build
# loads. This list named lavapipe and libvulkan only, from when lavapipe was
# the only driver here.
#
# ANGLE's is the one that actually fires: `rx::vk::CommandQueue::
# releaseFinishedCommandsLocked` runs on ANGLE's own command-queue thread and
# frees allocations the main thread made, and the happens-before that makes
# that safe is inside libGLESv2 where TSan cannot see it. What gets reported is
# a bare operator new / operator delete pair, attributed to the test binary
# because TSan interposes those - the only ctbrowser frame in the report is the
# allocator interposer itself.
#
# By LIBRARY, like everything else here, so a real race in our code is still
# caught with the driver below it on the stack.
race:libGLESv2.so
mutex:libGLESv2.so
deadlock:libGLESv2.so
called_from_lib:libGLESv2.so
race:libEGL.so
called_from_lib:libEGL.so
race:libvk_swiftshader.so
mutex:libvk_swiftshader.so
deadlock:libvk_swiftshader.so
called_from_lib:libvk_swiftshader.so
